        "evidence": "research/ai/2026-10-23-aggregation-families/proof.md",
        "section": "7",
        "statement": "For every positive integer n over every characteristic-zero field, an explicit 106-product balanced tripartition family proves rank(M(n^4,n^4,n^4)^direct_sum106)<=x^12+12*x^11+66*x^10+139*x^9+5*x^8, x=n+1. A separate set-based implementation checks all 1191016 mixed triples and 222 corrections. Compared with the credited external 105-product bound, 106*r105-105*r106=x^8*(x^4+12*x^3+66*x^2-1451*x-207). Substituting x=8+u gives coefficients 1,44,738,3957,2649, so the cost bound per output strictly improves for every integer n>=7.",
        "dependencies": [
          "Solomonik and Blaeser arXiv:2610.26563v2 centered aggregation and credited ex105 comparison witness",
